       val loaded = json.decodeFromString<List<OcrScreenshotEntry>>(text)\n489:             _entries.value = loaded\n490:             _lastEntry.value = loaded.lastOrNull()\n491:             version++\n492:         } catch (e: Exception) {\n493:             logcat(LogPriority.WARN, e) { \"OcrScreenshotBuffer: load failed\" }\n494:         }\n495:     }\n496: }\n\n(End of file - total 496 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                logcat(LogPriority.WARN, e) { \"OcrScreenshotBuffer: persist failed\" }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private fun load() {\n        val file = persistFile ?: return\n        if (!file.exists()) return\n        try {\n            val text = file.readText()\n            if (text.isBlank()) return\n            val loaded = json.decodeFromString<List<OcrScreenshotEntry>>(text)\n            _entries.value = loaded\n            _lastEntry.value = loaded.lastOrNull()\n            version++\n        } catch (e: Exception) {\n            logcat(LogPriority.WARN, e) { \"OcrScreenshotBuffer: load failed\" }\n        }", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt", "text": "\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                logcat(LogPriority.WARN, e) { \"OcrScreenshotBuffer: persist failed\" }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private fun load() {\n        val file = persistFile ?: return\n        if (!file.exists()) return\n        try {\n            val text = file.readText()\n            if (text.isBlank()) return\n            val loaded = json.decodeFromString<List<OcrScreenshotEntry>>(text)\n            _entries.value = loaded\n            _lastEntry.value = loaded.lastOrNull()\n            version++\n        } catch (e: Exception) {\n            logcat(LogPriority.WARN, e) { \"OcrScreenshotBuffer: load failed\" }\n        }\n    }\n}", "lineStart": 475, "lineEnd": 496, "totalLines": 496, "truncated": false}}, "title": "data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt", "time": {"start": 1791916601308, "end": 1791916601481}}, "id": "prt_1368d6fbb001SjH0a984uu6hHz", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368d618b001UMZRMRccCmxPUp"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_01_3vywqr71v38be11bry0fohga", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && grep -n \"ContextCompat\" app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/di/AppModule.kt; grep -n \"logcat\" app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt | head -3"}, "output": "6:import androidx.core.content.ContextCompat\n152:        ContextCompat.getMainExecutor(app).execute {\n58:import logcat.AndroidLogcatLogger\n59:import logcat.LogPriority\n60:import logcat.LogcatLogger\n", "metadata": {"output": "6:import androidx.core.content.ContextCompat\n152:        ContextCompat.getMainExecutor(app).execute {\n58:import logcat.AndroidLogcatLogger\n59:import logcat.LogPriority\n60:import logcat.LogcatLogger\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && grep -n \"ContextCompat\" app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/di/AppModule.kt; grep -n \"logcat\" app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt | head -3", "time": {"start": 1791916601414, "end": 1791916601446}}, "id": "prt_1368d6fde001TV1sTl0up2UevJ", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368d618b001UMZRMRccCmxPUp"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "192cc822868ba7841b5abf635bc5b9ebd779bb2b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 44154, "input": 1777, "output": 194, "reasoning": 71, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 42112}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1368d82dc001In2wqdBGNerC8s", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368d618b001UMZRMRccCmxPUp"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136851e9f001vbQSM6Hp2bsA9j", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 45316, "input": 707, "output": 161, "reasoning": 672, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 43776}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791916607093, "completed": 1791916617993}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1368d8675001pliVpxKISANry6", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "192cc822868ba7841b5abf635bc5b9ebd779bb2b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1368d934c001x15mBY4ZBUFi7q", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368d8675001pliVpxKISANry6"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "So `ContextCompat` only used at 152. Removing it means dropping the import to avoid unused import warning (spotless/detekt may fail on unused imports). Let me check other ContextCompat usages — grep found only line 6 and 152. So remove import too.\n\nOcrScreenshotBuffer.load() reads the whole JSON file synchronously. With up to 200 entries with region data (~1-5KB each) → up to ~1MB. That's real main-thread I/O. Moving `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` off main would help but the buffer is accessed by UI (StateFlow) — setting values from background is fine since it's a MutableStateFlow. But `init` sets `initialized` and directory. Doing it in a background thread with synchronization might race with early reads. Given the UI reads `_entries.value` (StateFlow, thread-safe), it's fine.\n\nBut wait: `init` is called in App.onCreate; if we background it, and the UI reads entries before load completes, it shows empty then updates. Fine.\n\nHowever, moving `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` off main requires care: `init` uses `mkdirs()` and `load()`. Safe on background. There's an `@Synchronized` on add but init isn't synchronized. If add() runs concurrently with init (unlikely at startup), race. Acceptable risk? The `initialized` flag isn't volatile... Let me not over-engineer; I could wrap init in a synchronized or run it on the same single-thread IO scope. OcrScreenshotBuffer has `scope` (Dispatchers.IO single thread) — but that's for persistence. I could post init to that scope. But `init` sets persistFile/imagesDir used by add. If add runs before init completes, imagesDir null → image not saved. At startup, auto-read likely not running yet.\n\nHmm. This is getting risky. The user said no regressions. Let me be conservative: the biggest win is AppModule. Let me also move the OcrVocabulary.configure read — but it's small (user words) and other code may need it immediately.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: is the UI slowness really about these? Let me look at MainActivity's `awaitAndRelease` runBlocking and the migrator, which the explore flagged. That's on main and blocks the very first frame. Let me read MainActivity around line 179.\n\nGiven time constraints and risk, I think the responsible move is:\n1. Fix AppModule main-executor (clear, safe, high-impact).\n2. Report the other startup issues with specifics and ask which to pursue (since some are architectural and could introduce regressions the user explicitly forbade).\n\nBut the user wants me to keep going. Let me look at MainActivity to gauge.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole situation. The user said \"ну что там\" and then system said continue. I've done the dictionary. I should probably also do the clear AppModule fix, then verify builds, then report and ask about the remaining bigger items (OCR chooser UX, manual region) since those need decisions.\n\nLet me read MainActivity:179 and MigrationJobFactory.", "time": {"start": 1791916610432, "end": 1791916616073}, "id": "prt_1368d9380001pp6bcxhLXUrL1F", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368d8675001pliVpxKISANry6"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "read", "callID": "call_00_945ried8k27wkh5y6kzdtoad", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"filePath": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/ui/main/MainActivity.kt", "limit": 45, "offset": 160}, "output": "<path>/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code/app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/ui/main/MainActivity.kt</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n160:         val splashScreen = if (isLaunch) installSplashScreen() else null\n161: \n162:         super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)\n163:         // v1.9.39: без runtime-разрешения POST_NOTIFICATIONS (API 33+) шторка\n164:         // оставалась пустой при сканировании — запрашиваем сразу.\n165:         if (android.os.Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 33 &&\n166:             checkSelfPermission(android.Manifest.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS) !=\n167:             android.content.pm.PackageManager.PERMISSION_GRANTED\n168:         ) {\n169:             requestPermissions(arrayOf(android.Manifest.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS), 4711)\n170:         }\n171: \n172:         // Модели OCR стартуют только после того, как разрешение на уведомления\n173:         // хоть раз спросили. Раньше загрузка на 21 МБ стартовала в\n174:         // Application.onCreate — раньше диалога разрешения, — поэтому её\n175:         // первые уведомления уходили в пустоту, а на Android 13+ notify()\n176:         // бросал SecurityException прямо в обработчик прогресса.\n177:         (application as? eu.kanade.tachiyomi.App)?.ensureOcrModelsInstalled()\n178: \n179:         Migrator.awaitAndRelease()\n180: \n181:         // Do not let the launcher create a new activity http://stackoverflow.com/questions/16283079\n182:         if (!isTaskRoot) {\n183:             finish()\n184:             return\n185:         }\n186: \n187:         setComposeContent {\n188:             val context = LocalContext.current\n189: \n190:             var incognito by remember { mutableStateOf(getIncognitoState.await(null)) }\n191:             val downloadOnly by preferences.downloadedOnly.collectAsState()\n192:             val indexing by downloadCache.isInitializing.collectAsState()\n193: \n194:     